# Ema Paper (repository `sightread`)

Canonical project rules (`.rule`; AGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md symlink here). This file is agent guardrails only — mechanisms, schemas, and behavior live in `docs/`, starting at `docs/index.md`.

## Docs first

- Read the docs matching the task before non-trivial work. Feature/schema/behavior changes: update `docs/` first, then implement; keep `docs/index.md` in sync.
- If a request conflicts with docs, state the conflict and wait for an explicit override.

## Cost safety — users' upstream keys are real money

- Never debug, reproduce, or benchmark against Kano Proxy, a user's provider connection, or any paid upstream. Verification is tests with stubbed HTTP (`docs/testing.md`). A live smoke test needs explicit per-instance approval: one tiny document, one cheap model, never a loop.

## Secrets

- Never commit secrets; real values live in `.env` (gitignored), tracked files use placeholders. Never print secret values — only whether one exists.
- Credential storage follows `docs/auth.md`. No credential material in logs or error messages, ever.

## Hard technical rules

- PDF work only via Poppler CLI subprocesses. No PyMuPDF, no linked PDF libraries (AGPL) — `docs/parsing.md`.
- The queue is PostgreSQL; do not introduce Redis or a message broker — `docs/jobs.md`.
- Uploads stream to disk with size caps, never buffered whole in memory; no `file path` source on hosted endpoints; uploads and SSE never route through the Nuxt server.
- Schema changes only via Alembic migrations (`alembic revision`, never hand-built files), `docs/database.md` updated first.
- No hard-coded environment values — URLs, hosts, TTLs, limits, paths go through `config.py` / env vars, mirrored in `.env.example`.
- Python via uv (`uv init`/`uv add`/`uv run`; never edit lockfiles by hand). Prefer official scaffold commands over hand-writing boilerplate in any ecosystem.
- Code, comments, identifiers in English; UI copy through the i18n catalog (en + zh-TW), never inline.

## Workflow

- Check existing files and `git status` before editing; never overwrite changes you didn't make.
- Before delivering: `uv run ruff check` + `uv run pytest` (api), `pnpm typecheck` + `pnpm lint` + `pnpm test` (web), `docker compose config` when compose files changed.
- The api tests need Linux (`os.O_PATH`, `/proc/self/fd`): on macOS run them in a Linux container (`ghcr.io/astral-sh/uv:python3.12-bookworm` with `poppler-utils` and `git`). Bound every test run with `timeout` and keep its output in view; a hung test otherwise runs unseen for hours.

## Real data only

- Frontend renders only what the backend returns; empty is a real state. Models come from the live catalog of the agent's upstream (Kano Proxy or a provider connection), usage from `usage_log` — never hard-coded as if live. Exceptions: test fixtures, docs examples with placeholders.
